WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.480
"Game of Thrones" is not exactly known for its&nbsp;
morally upstanding characters. This approach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:12.640
means that terms like "good" and "evil" mean very&nbsp;
little in the war-torn fantasy world of Westeros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:18.080
Characters who seem honorable and righteous&nbsp;
also make horrific choices and the dastardly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.680
so-called villains occasionally&nbsp;
perform acts of kindness and honor.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:26.720
With that in mind, Margaery Tyrell, played by&nbsp;
Natalie Dormer, has a lot in common with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:32.080
peers on the show. While always hungry for power,&nbsp;
like most characters on "Game of Thrones," she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.840
does possess kindness and understanding that is&nbsp;
quite uncommon among other royalty in Westeros.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.840
Still, no one is incapable of making terrible,&nbsp;
inexcusable choices, and Margaery is no different.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.240
“I am the Queen.”

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:51.840
In fact, there's one particular story arc&nbsp;
of hers that some would argue simply goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.080
way too far, even in this world of&nbsp;
murder, betrayal, and oppression.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.920
Margaery Tyrell is originally supposed to&nbsp;
marry the cruel and brutal Joffrey Baratheon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:07.680
played by Jack Gleeson. However, upon his&nbsp;
assassination, she marries Tommen Baratheon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:13.760
played by Dean-Charles Chapman instead. Tommen is&nbsp;
far kinder than his brother but more susceptible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.600
to manipulation because of his young age and&nbsp;
naivety. Margaery uses this to her advantage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.160
and emotionally manipulates the young king&nbsp;
into doing everything she wants. It's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:30.080
truly uncomfortable relationship, and every scene&nbsp;
between the two characters is difficult to watch.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:36.480
Eventually, after Margaery is killed by Tommen's&nbsp;
mother, Cersei, Tommen dies by suicide by jumping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.200
from a tower. While it's clear that his&nbsp;
mother, with her thirst for power above all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.920
else, shares responsibility for this, the&nbsp;
deeply problematic relationship between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.640
Margaery and Tommen is at fault too. The&nbsp;
fact that it ends so tragically is not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.080
a testament to how realistic "Game of Thrones"&nbsp;
can be at times. It’s also another indicator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.040
of just how grim and unrelenting the show is&nbsp;
when it comes to killing off its characters.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.840
So was it worth it for Margaery? The young&nbsp;
woman successfully becomes Queen of the Seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:11.680
Kingdoms through her marriage to Joffrey, and then&nbsp;
Tommen, but it's quite a short reign. She easily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.800
gains control of Tommen, who falls in love with&nbsp;
her, but she can't beat Cersei's manipulations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.440
which lead the Faith Militant to arrest&nbsp;
her brother Loras and then her. Tommen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.520
without enough knowledge about the world&nbsp;
of politics and how to use his power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.440
is unable to save his wife or&nbsp;
handle the emotional aftermath.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.920
Tommen's history of being coddled by his&nbsp;
mother and abused by his older brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:40.640
shapes him into the innocent and ill-prepared king&nbsp;
he becomes. Likewise, Margaery's manipulative ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:46.720
are definitely created by those who raised her. In&nbsp;
her case, the most influential person in her life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.480
is arguably Olenna Tyrell, her grandmother and&nbsp;
the matriarch of the Tyrell line. We all know how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:58.240
cunning the old woman is, successfully murdering&nbsp;
Joffrey at his own wedding and framing Tyrion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:03.280
in order to get Margaery on the throne. This in&nbsp;
turn leads to her marriage to Tommen. You could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:09.280
even argue that Olenna is to blame for Margaery's&nbsp;
death, although this is undoubtedly unintentional.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.120
Olenna truly loves her granddaughter&nbsp;
and would do anything to protect her.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:19.280
Margaery has ambitious dreams born from Olenna's&nbsp;
guidance, and she knows how to manipulate people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.840
especially men, in order to get what she&nbsp;
wants. She's taught that power and control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.280
is the main goal in life — no matter the&nbsp;
cost — which Olenna continuously encourages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.800
While Margaery appears to actually be a good&nbsp;
person and care for Tommen, she is too blinded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:40.720
the influences of her family and the psychological&nbsp;
warfare going on in King's Landing. Margaery tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:46.800
to manipulate Tommen while still keeping him safe.&nbsp;
However, in the end her own goals remain the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.560
priority and Margaery uses Tommen as a pawn,&nbsp;
leading him down the path to his horrific fate.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.640
Compared to other characters in&nbsp;
"Game of Thrones," especially Cersei,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.400
Margaery seems like a saint. But is&nbsp;
she just as bad as the rest of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.240
for the death her manipulations&nbsp;
cause, or is she also a victim?

